    <string name="direct_links">Direct Wi-Fi links</string>
    <string name="direct_links_why">When a transfer you start or accept runs through the relay, todoke can move it onto a Wi-Fi link straight between the two devices: faster, and no internet needed. Android asks for permission to find nearby Wi-Fi devices for that. todoke never uses it to find your location, and only during a transfer.</string>
    <string name="direct_links_off">Off: transfers use your network or the relay.</string>
    <string name="pointing">Point to share</string>
    <string name="pointing_why">Point this phone at a nearby device to pick it. Android asks for permission to measure the distance and direction to nearby devices with ultra-wideband for that. todoke uses it only while you point, or while a contact points at this phone with todoke open.</string>
